# Foundation Mathematics Course — Implementation Plan

## Goal

Build the complete **Foundation Mathematics** course module under the **Mathematics for Computer Scientists** track in the `gasigwa-portfolio` project. The course is sourced from PDF screenshots of lecture notes and transcribed into structured markdown lesson files, each paired with an interactive multiple-choice quiz.

---

## Architecture

### Content Files

All lesson markdown files live in:

```
public/lessons/mathematics-for-computer-scientists/foundation-mathematics/
```

Each file follows the naming convention: `chapter-N[-part]-slug.md`

### Quiz Files

All quiz JavaScript modules live in:

```
src/data/quizzes/
```

Naming convention: `foundation-math-chN[-part]-quiz.js`
Every quiz file **must** include `export default <quizName>;` at the bottom.

### Registration Files

- **`src/data/quizzes/index.js`** — imports all quiz files and exports them in the `quizzes` map.
- **`src/data/lessons.jsx`** — registers each chapter page under the `foundation-mathematics` section with a `slug`, `title`, `summary`, and `quiz` key.

