### Chapter 6 — Permutations and Combinations (Split into 2 parts)

#### [NEW] chapter-6-1-permutations.md

Covers: Fundamental counting principle; factorial notation (n!); permutation formula ⁿPᵣ = n!/(n-r)!; arrangements with restrictions (subtraction method); circular permutations (n-1)!; permutations with repeated objects (n!/k!).

#### [NEW] chapter-6-2-combinations.md

Covers: Combinations vs permutations (key distinction table); combination formula ⁿCᵣ = n!/((n-r)!×r!); derivation from permutations; worked examples (cards, hockey team); useful properties (symmetry property, Pascal's Identity); decision guide for choosing the correct method.

